                        "entry_id": "0ffd891c-1a03-36d4-a991-5c1f9ce505a7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling or having feelings of Christmas; festive."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d5e28bf-79ad-432d-bc30-0890d53fd78b",
                                "sense_id": "20dcffda-893e-3b22-b7eb-c73f4ec4024e",
                                "text": "It is important to guard against any hint of a generalisation here that 'less Christmassy music' always accompanies a 'less Christmassy sentiment', and indeed Greg Lake's 'I Believe In Father Christmas' (1974) is proof that the converse is not […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "40e98ad5-3a7f-4968-acba-48a803a356be",
                                "sense_id": "20dcffda-893e-3b22-b7eb-c73f4ec4024e",
                                "text": "Mark: That looks like a lovely turkey. I'm sorry I flew off the handle a bit.\nJeremy: That wasn't very Christmassy.\nMark: No, it wasn't. I apologise."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3c1b9017-bdf1-4b27-8cef-1a246674b9e7",
                                "sense_id": "20dcffda-893e-3b22-b7eb-c73f4ec4024e",
                                "text": "They [Asian pears] are unquestionably Christmassy and festive, with their golden speckled skin."
                            }
                        ]
